{"id":"ab39e4b6-5a72-4cd5-8af8-a1c2b787c57b","object":"chat.completion","created":1791535954,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Two concrete validation issues: `evidence_used` capped at 12 (I sent 13) and `scope` must be a list. Correcting only those.","reasoning_content":"Two concrete corrections:\n1. evidence_used max 12 items → merge one (combine task_success and validity into one, or drop one).\n2. scope must be a list.\n\nLet me fix: reduce evidence_used to 12 by merging the \"validity\" and \"task_success\" facts into one fact? They have different pointers. I'll merge them into a single fact with pointer \"/validity\" and value \"valid\", statement covering both... but pointer must be exact. Better: drop one fact. I'll merge the two evaluation facts (validity + task_success) into one using pointer \"/task_success\"? Hmm, each fact has a single pointer. I'll just remove the separate \"/validity\" fact and fold its mention into the task_success fact statement. Actually cleaner: remove the \"/validity\" fact and instead include validity in a merged statement with pointer \"/task_success\"... that misattributes. Let me instead remove the \"/validity\" fact entirely (12 items) and mention validity in reason (already mentioned). Validity is also covered by the acceptance component evaluation_validity. Good.\n\nWait, count: I have 13 facts. Remove the \"/validity\" one → 12.\n\n3. scope as list: scope = [ ... ] list of objects with identity fields. Probably list of source identity dicts. I'll make scope a list containing one object with the identity fields, or a list of {\"field\":..., \"value\":...}? \"scope contains inspected source identity fields.\" Likely a list of identity entries. I'll provide a list of objects each with reference/pointer and identity fields? Safer: list of strings? Hmm.\n\nGiven uncertainty, I'll use a list of objects each with identity field name/value and a source reference. Actually simpler: scope: [{\"artifact_id\": \"...\", \"candidate_id\": \"fixed-radius\", \"comparison_identity\": \"...\", \"evaluator\": \"evaluate.reach\", \"evaluator_version\": \"1.0.0\", \"original_execution_id\": \"...\", \"source_execution_id\": \"...\", \"validity\": \"valid\", \"task_identity\": \"...\"}].\n\nI'll go with a list containing one dict of identity fields, plus include a second entry for other identities (task/robot). Let's do two entries: one for the evaluation source identity, one for the execution/task identity.\n\nLet me resubmit with these two fixes only.\n\nAlso the report reference: fine.\n\nLet me rebuild the decision with evidence_used = 12 items and scope as list.\n\nAlso note: revise remaining_unknowns fine.\n\nSubmit revision 1 again? The revision key is stable across delivery IDs; the failed submission presumably didn't commit. I'll use revision 1.\n\nHmm — should I use revision 2? \"A revision key is stable across delivery IDs.\" The instruction says submit with revision 1. The validation error means it wasn't accepted. I'll keep revision 1.\n\nLet me construct.","tool_calls":[{"index":0,"id":"call_00_cLtIvcLMXLB5RgR4WSQN6385","type":"function","function":{"name":"submit_result","arguments":"{\"revision\": 1, \"decision\": {\"adopted_claims\": [{\"scope\": [{\"artifact_id\": \"6314170dd823eab26d13296eb5afee1cfe24cb2f5117334414d1d66e8d266892\", \"candidate_id\": \"fixed-radius\", \"comparison_identity\": \"3c24b89e5c9abc7589dc69839f25d5050be1b212d31a2dec86dba230198c92c8\", \"evaluator\": \"evaluate.reach\", \"evaluator_version\": \"1.0.0\", \"original_execution_id\": \"197bceb6ff8f44b48a35bc4f79b3528d\", \"source_execution_id\": \"197bceb6ff8f44b48a35bc4f79b3528d\", \"validity\": \"valid\"}], \"statement\": \"The saved official reach error recorded for the fixed-C (candidate 'fixed-radius') execution is 0.0031314437885609334 m (position_error, in metres).\", \"support_explanation\": \"The extraction-only report records exactly one fact: statement 'Saved official reach error', value 0.0031314437885609334, at pointer /metrics/0/value of source 6314170d…6892. The directly read original of that source confirms metrics[0] = {name: position_error, units: m, value: 0.0031314437885609334}. The adopted claim is deliberately restricted to this recorded reach-error value; it asserts neither joint acceptance nor robot-task success.\", \"supporting_facts\": [{\"pointer\": \"/metrics/0/value\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"6314170dd823eab26d13296eb5afee1cfe24cb2f5117334414d1d66e8d266892\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Saved official reach error\", \"value\": 0.0031314437885609334}]}], \"disposition\": \"accept\", \"evidence_used\": [{\"pointer\": \"/constraints/0\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"6314170dd823eab26d13296eb5afee1cfe24cb2f5117334414d1d66e8d266892\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Saved evaluation constraint task_bound: limit 0.01 m, observed 0.0031314437885609334 m, satisfied true\", \"value\": {\"limit\": 0.01, \"name\": \"task_bound\", \"observed\": 0.0031314437885609334, \"satisfied\": true, \"units\": \"m\"}}, {\"pointer\": \"/validity\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"6314170dd823eab26d13296eb5afee1cfe24cb2f5117334414d1d66e8d266892\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Saved evaluation recorded validity 'valid' with reason null and task_success true (historical arrival-only evaluator evaluate.reach)\", \"value\": \"valid\"}, {\"pointer\": \"/detail/sampled_settling\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"400226bfd9f0d75d698037f494987054f3030fce7813612c11f6f4d4e5d6ab13\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Holding-window report: sampled settling available with continuous_time_guarantee false, position_limit_m 0.01, speed_limit_m_s 0.02, window_s 0.05, and passed false\", \"value\": {\"available\": true, \"continuous_time_guarantee\": false, \"max_error_m\": 0.0033622899352609014, \"max_speed_m_s\": 0.026817670846968282, \"passed\": false, \"position_limit_m\": 0.01, \"speed_limit_m_s\": 0.02, \"window_s\": 0.05}}, {\"pointer\": \"/detail/sampled_settling/max_speed_m_s\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"400226bfd9f0d75d698037f494987054f3030fce7813612c11f6f4d4e5d6ab13\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Holding-window report: maximum sampled holding-window tip speed 0.026817670846968282 m/s exceeds the 0.02 m/s speed limit\", \"value\": 0.026817670846968282}, {\"pointer\": \"/detail/sampled_settling/max_error_m\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"400226bfd9f0d75d698037f494987054f3030fce7813612c11f6f4d4e5d6ab13\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Holding-window report: maximum sampled holding-window tip position error 0.0033622899352609014 m is within the 0.01 m position limit\", \"value\": 0.0033622899352609014}, {\"pointer\": \"/detail/motion_summary\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"400226bfd9f0d75d698037f494987054f3030fce7813612c11f6f4d4e5d6ab13\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Holding-window report: terminal tip speed 0.021786196764909577 m/s and terminal tip error 0.003131443788560934 m at tolerance_m 0.01\", \"value\": {\"minimum_sampled_error_m\": 0.0030266910650862838, \"terminal_error_m\": 0.003131443788560934, \"terminal_tip_speed_m_s\": 0.021786196764909577, \"tolerance_m\": 0.01}}, {\"pointer\": \"/detail/status\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"5582561d4de48e4450f5619024d2a92296a6f7ed12c77c470cd8d573aa588627\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Joint-acceptance record: accepted false with status valid_failure under protocol offline_reach_hold_v1\", \"value\": \"valid_failure\"}, {\"pointer\": \"/detail/components/holding_speed\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"5582561d4de48e4450f5619024d2a92296a6f7ed12c77c470cd8d573aa588627\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Joint-acceptance component holding_speed: limit 0.02 m/s, passed false, value 0.026817670846968282 m/s\", \"value\": {\"limit\": 0.02, \"passed\": false, \"reason\": null, \"unit\": \"m/s\", \"value\": 0.026817670846968282}}, {\"pointer\": \"/detail/components/holding_position\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"5582561d4de48e4450f5619024d2a92296a6f7ed12c77c470cd8d573aa588627\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Joint-acceptance component holding_position: limit 0.01 m, passed true, value 0.0033622899352609014 m\", \"value\": {\"limit\": 0.01, \"passed\": true, \"reason\": null, \"unit\": \"m\", \"value\": 0.0033622899352609014}}, {\"pointer\": \"/detail/official_recorded_task_success\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"5582561d4de48e4450f5619024d2a92296a6f7ed12c77c470cd8d573aa588627\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Joint-acceptance record: official_recorded_task_success true while composite acceptance is false (new_backend_solves 0, continuous_time_guarantee false)\", \"value\": true}, {\"pointer\": \"/detail/execution_id\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"5582561d4de48e4450f5619024d2a92296a6f7ed12c77c470cd8d573aa588627\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Joint-acceptance execution identity: execution_id 197bceb6ff8f44b48a35bc4f79b3528d bound to task_identity d0f438cf0a0149adba72f8358cdcbbe21ddd5a32fbd066c5a9f03d7f092e2df7\", \"value\": \"197bceb6ff8f44b48a35bc4f79b3528d\"}, {\"pointer\": \"/detail/execution_scope\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"400226bfd9f0d75d698037f494987054f3030fce7813612c11f6f4d4e5d6ab13\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Holding-window report execution scope robot identity 0a0bad0e7e50ba6329801c180c5dc7466617de865ce373e6f0bb494637a88306 at seed 17, task family task.reach, goal target_m [0.29, 0.035, 0.19]\", \"value\": {\"goal_target_m\": [0.29, 0.035, 0.19], \"robot_identity\": \"0a0bad0e7e50ba6329801c180c5dc7466617de865ce373e6f0bb494637a88306\", \"seed\": 17}}], \"investigation_id\": \"fixed-C-offline-report\", \"reason\": \"Disposition 'accept' endorses the extraction-only report's single recorded fact and the validity of the saved evidence bundle; it does NOT assert joint acceptance or robot-task success. Outcome of the four criteria for the saved fixed-C execution (evaluation 6314170d…6892; profile 400226bf…6ab13; joint-acceptance record 5582561d…8627; all bound to execution 197bceb6ff8f44b48a35bc4f79b3528d and task identity d0f438cf0a0149adba72f8358cdcbbe21ddd5a32fbd066c5a9f03d7f092e2df7): the execution is complete and valid (execution_complete true, evaluation_validity 'valid', solver_errors 0). (1) ARRIVAL satisfied: terminal tip position error 0.0031314437885609334 m <= 0.01 m task bound; the historical evaluator evaluate.reach@1.0.0 recorded task_success true and the profile recorded terminal_error_m 0.003131443788560934 m. (2) HOLDING POSITION satisfied: maximum sampled holding-window tip error 0.0033622899352609014 m <= 0.01 m position limit (component holding_position passed true). (3) HOLDING SPEED NOT satisfied: maximum sampled holding-window tip speed 0.026817670846968282 m/s > 0.02 m/s speed limit (component holding_speed passed false), and the terminal tip speed 0.021786196764909577 m/s also exceeds 0.02 m/s; holding_coverage passed with 6 inclusive uniform samples over window_s 0.05. (4) JOINT ACCEPTANCE FAILED: accepted false, status 'valid_failure' under protocol_id 'offline_reach_hold_v1' (research.task_acceptance@1.0.0), because one component (holding_speed) fails even though official_recorded_task_success is true. Hence arrival and holding position are met, holding speed is not, and joint acceptance is not achieved; the historical arrival-only task success must not be read as joint success. Scope limitations: sampled observations give no continuous-time guarantee and no causal attribution; ideal-tension modelling and omitted dynamics preclude physical conclusions; the result applies only to this candidate/seed/target/execution, so a different candidate or an identified cause of the speed exceedance remains unassessed. No new computation, backend solve or robot experiment was performed for this judgment (new_backend_solves 0).\", \"remaining_unknowns\": [\"Physical cause of the holding-window speed exceedance is not identified by the saved sampled observations.\", \"Live-model compatibility and physical-robot behaviour are unassessed; the model uses ideal tensions and omits shear, stretch, torsion, tendon friction and actuator dynamics.\", \"Continuous-time holding behaviour is not guaranteed (continuous_time_guarantee false; window_s 0.05 sampled as 6 inclusive uniform samples).\", \"Results cover only candidate 'fixed-radius' (fixed-C) at seed 17 in execution 197bceb6ff8f44b48a35bc4f79b3528d for target [0.29, 0.035, 0.19] with tolerance 0.01 m; other candidates, seeds and targets are unassessed.\", \"Nested referenced artifacts (simulation/source e2c5a5ed18220463ac6583996a18351cdd978b879e54e5820ebaa6165979b9cd, motion 27c1929fbe449905b8a420d500c87677ada6d246f808a507d1dade8c8f818bd0, configuration 77a1406779dbbf5c440e8077796eeb222446001587d1a9befea0c64bbc146925, one-step-prediction evidence 1e7ac5866379f5db5f24f7e07152b961fd5f45ed527ffbc81cb01a3f25cfd557) were not independently readable and were not used to support any claim.\", \"Real-time behaviour was not demonstrated (real_time_demonstrated false; deadline_misses 35 of 35 updates; mean_update_s 12.331832479999866 s versus control_period_s 0.01 s).\"], \"report\": {\"artifact_id\": \"66ff0f1c550ccd2117f33d64831ac206629a3858b01e50fb97fefc5106153abf\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}}}"}}]},"logprobs":null,"finish_r